M07 follow-ups to the soft-lock hunt (2026-10-07). Four small, saved,
once-only guards; every normal-path callback still runs the original code.

1. M07_Climb_Rope: the inn-evac climb (S_A_Human.XG_EV5_Troop, 30 frames at
   15 fps) only finished on a NORMAL Play_Animation completion. A preempted
   climb, or one that does not resume after a mid-climb save/load, would leave
   Hotwire on the rope; M07_Hotwire_Dead then fails the mission. Add a saved
   climb_finished flag (ID 1) and a 10 s CLIMB_ROPE_FALLBACK timer (timers are
   saved) that finishes the climb once. On the normal path the evacuee is
   destroyed after 2 s and the timer never fires.
2. M07_Objective_Controller: M07_CON001 (key) only acted on ENDED. Stopped
   early (Havoc beyond the 200 m audience radius, or UNABLE_TO_INIT), objectives
   701/710, the nuke countdown and the team assembly order were all skipped.
   Run the same block once (saved briefing_done, ID 3) from a 1 s timer when
   Havoc and Gunner are still alive, so a dead orator or a teardown stop never
   acts.
3. M07_Dead6_Engineer: a LOW_PRIORITY ARRIVE_EVAC_SPOT completion left Hotwire
   idle at 4 of 5 inn evacuees. Retry the goto from a 2 s timer (a rejection is
   notified synchronously inside M07_Inn_Evac::Custom, so it never reports
   from there), and report M07_DEAD6_EVAC once only (saved evac_reported,
   ID 9), so M07_CON017 cannot be started twice.
4. M07_Para_Drop_Controller: para_drop[] was set in Created only and not saved,
   so after a load the troop drops used zero ids and landed at the origin.
   Save it (ID 8, unused) and re-seed the same constant table when a save made
   before this change restored nothing.

